name w4-07-cap-intercept
timeout 600
time 1999-03-26T10:00:00Z
wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

# CAMPAIGN W4, SORTIE 7 OF 10 - ALLIED FORCE 1999. THE 127th's AIRCRAFT, AS THEY ACTUALLY WERE.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w4-allied-force.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none. This file's own control is INSIDE it: two MiG-29s, identical but for one line.
#
# THE ANCHOR: the 127th Fighter Aviation Squadron "Knights" at Batajnica scrambled five MiG-29s on the
# night of 24/25 March 1999 and lost several to F-15Cs on 24/25 and 26 March; the surviving aircraft
# had "outdated avionics, degraded radar performance and a limited missile stock" [T4]. W4's spec
# expresses the degradation as `set n019_mode off` on ONE of the pair, and asks what an opponent with
# no radar at all still does to a flight. THE FULL BATAJNICA MATERIAL LIVES IN o5-airfield-defence.md
# §Knowledge 1 and is not duplicated here.
#
# THE ONE LINE THAT DIFFERS between `k7mig1` and `k7mig2` is `set n019_mode rad` against
# `set n019_mode off`. Everything else - spawn geometry mirrored about the ingress line, stores, the
# briefed GCI, the emission policy - is identical, so this file is a controlled pair inside one run
# and needs no sibling.
#
# THE EMISSION POLICY IS DECLARED IN ADVANCE, because rule 11 says a result that contradicts an
# earlier campaign is a different QUANTITY until proved otherwise, and the deciding line for a MiG-29
# is `set n019_emission`, not `set brief_gci` (O2 §State; W3 flew both sides). BOTH MiGs here fly the
# documented power-up state `off` and both carry the same three-entry brief, so the radar is turned on
# by the controller's third typed entry - on the jet that has a radar.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION: none on either side. The F-16C and the MiG-29 (9-12) are both this anchor's own
# types, which makes sortie 07 one of the two files in the whole campaign that needs no substitution
# statement. No catalogue row flies (see the campaign file).
#
# THE ALTITUDE SPLIT IS DELIBERATE AND IT IS THIS CAMPAIGN'S ONE PLACE WHERE THE WEATHER BITES: the
# CAP flies at 8,000/8,150 m and the MiGs at 5,000/5,150 m, so the fixture's mid deck (ceiling 6,861 m
# at this point, 72.6 % mid cover) stands BETWEEN them. Both MiGs carry `set kols_mode ir` +
# `set kols_laser on`, because the KOLS is the blind jet's only remaining sensor and because
# `FBVisualSystem`'s transmittance march is the ONLY consumer of cloud in the tree (`C16`). A first cut
# of this file had both sides at 6,000 m, under the deck, and produced zero masked lines - i.e. the
# cloud is only weather when something looks THROUGH it.
#
# THE ARENA, [SET] in the Kosovo engagement zone; the ground set is the field the CAP stands over -
# `k7nod` a radiating P-18, `k7hgr` a hardened shelter, `k7tgt` the field's own vehicle park. NOTHING
# ON THE GROUND IS ATTACKED IN THIS FILE: it is what the CAP is there for, and it is declared so that
# the fight has a reason to be where it is (INDEX rule 3).
#
# THE FOUR STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES: see w4-01-floor.fbm. Note #4 especially: this is an air engagement
# and the run ends at the first flight-monitor K.O.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT DOES A FIGHTER WITH NO RADAR STILL DO TO A FLIGHT - AND DOES THE
# F-16 PILOT NOTICE THAT IT IS NEVER ILLUMINATED?
#
# READING RULE (binding): the exit code is not the verdict. Read (1) `n019` contacts and launch
# solutions per MiG, (2) `rwr THREAT_NEW/THREAT_MODE` on the two F-16s - the second half of the
# question is whether the blind MiG ever appears on a Viper's receiver at all, (3) `irst` lines on the
# blind MiG: the KOLS is the only sensor it has left, (4) who shot whom and at what miss distance. Do
# NOT read kills as the lever's effect - read the DETECTION times.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 2757c699583ca1de, exit 3): A FIGHTER WITH NO RADAR DOES NOTHING, AND THE
# FLIGHT NEVER LEARNS IT IS THERE.
#   what each Viper heard   `k7capa`: symbol 1 (`surface-search`, the P-18, t=0.1) and symbol 2
#                     (`fire-control`, t=28.0, dropped t=84.7). `k7capb`: the same two, plus symbol 3
#                     at t=64.5 which is the SAME emitter re-acquired after a scan gap and which then
#                     walks `search -> track` (t=82.7) `-> missile` (t=102.6). **ONE fire-control
#                     emitter, for a pair of MiG-29s.** The blind jet never produces a symbol, so the
#                     answer to the second half of the question is that the F-16 does not notice it is
#                     never illuminated - it cannot even count the opposition
#   the serviceable jet   `k7mig1` fires one R-27R at t=102.5 from 13.0 km and is killed at t=111.8 by
#                     an AIM-120 at **2.08 m**; a second AIM-120 arrives at 0.22 m on the wreck
#   the blind jet     `k7mig2`: **zero radar contacts, zero IRST contacts, zero launches**, survives to
#                     TIMEOUT. Its KOLS is powered and armed (`irst LASER armed=1` at t=0.0) and finds
#                     nothing, because the only thing it could have found was above a cloud deck
#   THE CLOUD, AND THIS IS THE ONE PLACE IN THE WHOLE CAMPAIGN WHERE IT IS MEASURED:
#                     `vis MASKED unit=k7mig2 sizeMrad=5.098 transmittance=8.00571e-13 azDeg=53.2` at
#                     t=123.0 - not attenuation, an optically CLOSED path, integrated by
#                     `core/FBCloudDensity` between a MiG at 5,150 m and an F-16 at 8,000 m with the
#                     fixture's 72.6 % mid deck (ceiling 6,861 m) in between. `k7mig1`, 1,000 m higher
#                     in the same air, gets a `vis CONTACT` at 6.58 mrad instead
#   SO WHAT IS MEASURED OF THIS CAMPAIGN'S BAD WEATHER, IN FULL: the WIND, priced at 5.014 m of bomb
#   miss per knot (sortie 02), and ONE line of sight closed to 8e-13 (this file). Everything else the
#   deck does in the anchor - hiding targets from a bomber, hiding a battery from a Weasel, sending a
#   package home with its bombs - is `C16` and is not modelled.
#   THE ANCHOR'S OWN VERDICT is that the 127th lost aircraft on 24-26 March and did no damage in
#   return. This file reproduces the shape (1 lost, 0 scored) with a serviceable jet that at least
#   shoots, and the campaign notes the direction: FlightBox's MiG-29 has a working look-down radar and
#   a better warning receiver than the 1999 aircraft, so Red here is STRONGER than history.

unit k7capa
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight cap7 1
  spawn 42.70000 20.60000 8000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set iff_interrogator on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 42.70000 21.40000 8000 480
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit k7capb
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight cap7 2
  spawn 42.66000 20.60000 8150 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set iff_interrogator on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 42.66000 21.40000 8150 480
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit k7mig1
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight kn7 1
  spawn 42.70000 21.50000 5000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad                          # THE SERVICEABLE JET
  set n019_range_nm 54
  set n019_emission off
  set kols_mode ir                            # the KOLS is ON in both jets: it is the blind one's ONLY sensor
  set kols_laser on
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r73
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 270 100 0
  set brief_gci 60 270 70 0
  set brief_gci 100 270 45 0
  wp 42.70000 20.55000 5000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive

unit k7mig2
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight kn7 2
  spawn 42.66000 21.50000 5150 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode off                          # THE ONE LINE: no radar at all
  set n019_range_nm 54
  set n019_emission off
  set kols_mode ir                            # the KOLS is ON in both jets: it is the blind one's ONLY sensor
  set kols_laser on
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r73
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 270 100 0
  set brief_gci 60 270 70 0
  set brief_gci 100 270 45 0
  wp 42.66000 20.55000 5150 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive

unit k7nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 42.62000 21.55000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free

unit k7hgr
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 42.60000 21.52000 ground 90.0 0

unit k7tgt
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 42.61000 21.56000 ground 90.0 0
